-- Alice and Bob each mean to buy dinner tonight, and neither wants to buy it
-- if the other already has. Alice checks whether dinner is bought and, if her
-- check found it unbought, buys. If Bob buys between her check and her
-- purchase, two dinners are bought. The file is wrong on purpose.
--
-- Alice and Bob are the two sides of a RAND, and Alice's side reads the
-- record Bob's side makes. Before smucclaw/l4-ide#1069 L4 ran one side over
-- the whole trace before the other, so `l4 explore` said the property held
-- (it does not: Alice checks at 10, Bob buys at 11, Alice buys at 12). Now
-- the two sides take the trace's events in step, so Alice's purchase at 12
-- sees Bob's at 11, `l4 run` records `open at acceptance` IS FALSE, and
-- `l4 explore` finds the race.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Alice, Bob

DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `checks whether dinner is bought`
    `buys dinner`

DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    opened     -- nobody has bought dinner
    taken      -- Bob has

DECLARE Dinner IS ONE OF
    `dinner for two`

`closing` MEANS 100

§ `Reading the ledgers`

GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ledger is open` MEANS NOT (elem taken `dinner status record`)

GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A Status
`the ledger's status` MEANS
    IF elem taken `dinner status record` THEN taken ELSE opened

§ `The evening`

-- Dinner starts unbought; then Alice and Bob act independently, at the same time.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the arrangement` MEANS
    COMMIT `dinner status record` IS opened
    HENCE `Alice's evening` RAND `Bob's evening`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Alice's evening` MEANS
    PARTY Alice
    MAY   `checks whether dinner is bought`
    WITHIN 0 OF closing
    HENCE RECORD Alice's `belief` IS `the ledger's status` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
          HENCE `Alice decides`
    LEST  FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Alice decides` MEANS
    PARTY Alice
    MAY   `buys dinner` PROVIDED (RECALL Alice's `belief`) EQUALS JUST opened
    WITHIN 0 OF closing
    HENCE COMMIT `dinners bought` IS `dinner for two`
          HENCE COMMIT `open at acceptance` IS `the ledger is open` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
          HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Bob's evening` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY   `buys dinner` PROVIDED `the ledger is open` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
    WITHIN 0 OF closing
    HENCE COMMIT `dinner status record` IS taken
          HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  FULFILLED

§ `The property`

GIVEN `open at acceptance` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every dinner was accepted while open` MEANS all (GIVEN ok YIELD ok) `open at acceptance`

#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES `checks whether dinner is bought` AT 10
    PARTY Bob   DOES `buys dinner`                     AT 11
    PARTY Alice DOES `buys dinner`                     AT 12
